# Line-ending policy for agent-godot-wrapper (inherited from agent-unity-wrapper
# ticket #29).
#
# Claude Code silently ignores instruction/skill/settings files checked out
# with CRLF, and because the committed blobs are LF the damage is invisible to
# `git status` / `git diff` - only `git update-index --refresh` reveals it.
#
# A repo-wide LF default is used instead of an enumerated allowlist so that
# files added later (e.g. a new .claude/agents/*.md) are covered by
# construction; an allowlist would re-introduce exactly the bug this file
# exists to prevent.
#
# gitattributes take precedence over core.autocrlf, so this holds on Windows
# clones and worktrees with core.autocrlf=true. This file is also staged onto
# the orphan `release` branch by .github/workflows/release.yml, so plugin
# installs on Windows get an LF SKILL.md too.

# Default: auto-detect text, normalize to LF in the index, check out LF
# in the working tree on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bash refuses to run a script with CRLF; PowerShell and Python are fine on LF.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF - cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only labels and
# goto targets. Defensive: no such files exist today.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary: never EOL-converted, never diffed. assets/icon.png is a release
# artifact served raw from raw.githubusercontent.com at the release tag, so a
# rewritten blob would ship a broken marketplace listing image.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.zip  binary
